<title>RUSSIA: Iraq oil deal to fully observe UN sanctions - Russia.</title>
<headline>Iraq oil deal to fully observe UN sanctions - Russia.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Russian-Iraqi accord to tap southern Iraq's Qurana oilfield will not involve any drilling, output or other work on the ground until U.N. sanctions are lifted, Russian officials involved in the deal said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The U.N. sanctions will be fully observed,&quot; said Zarubezhneft deputy chairman Yuri Agababov, whose firm has a stake in the deal.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not looking to violate any sanctions. The only things that will go forward now are things that do not violate the sanctions,&quot; he said, citing feasibility studies and early talks with lending institutions.</p>
</text>
